  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Making Sense: Language, Ethics, and Understanding in Deaf Nepal (2024), published by University of California Press, has been cited 1 time. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 1,342 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Making Sense: Language, Ethics, and Understanding in Deaf Nepal by E. Mara Green was published by University of California Press in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Linguistics, Psychology, Sociology and Philosophy. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) — Anthropology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 1 citation. Notable citing venues include Social Science & Medicine. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,342 times via OAPEN and Ubiquity Press. It is recorded in 2 library collections. Its subject matter aligns with Quality Education among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 1 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
